      "content": "hey, i'm looking at some logs from our staging environment and i'm seeing a lot of these SettingWithCopyWarning alerts popping up during our nightly ETL jobs. \n\nIt's happening in this block:\n```python\nfiltered_data = df[df['status'] == 'active']\nfiltered_data['processed'] = True\n```\n\nI know it's technically just a warning, but in a production pipeline, it feels like a major red flag. Does this warning actually signify a real threat to the integrity of the original dataframe, or is it just pandas being overly cautious? I need to know how much of a risk this \"warning\" actually poses to our data consistency before I clear it.",
